  {
    "turn": 3,
    "response": "I see the issue. The function `duration_minutes` calculates `sign * hours * 60 + minutes`, which means for negative durations with nonzero minutes, the sign only applies to the hours part, not the minutes.\n\nFor example:\n- `duration_minutes(-1, 0, 30)` returns `-0 * 60 + 30 = 30` (should be `-30`)\n- `duration_minutes(-1, 1, 30)` returns `-1 * 60 + 30 = -30` (correct)\n\nThe fix should be `sign * (hours * 60 + minutes)` to apply the sign to the entire magnitude.\n\n<tool_call>\n<function=edit>\n<parameter=path>\nduration.py\n</parameter>\n<parameter=old_string>\ndef duration_minutes(sign, hours, minutes):\n    return sign * hours * 60 + minutes\n</parameter>\n<parameter=new_string>\ndef duration_minutes(sign, hours, minutes):\n    return sign * (hours * 60 + minutes)\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>",
